\staccatissimo is not a command that can be executed on
its own. It is highlighted in the editor, but running it
gives an "unknown command" error.

A staccatissimo is written after a note with a hyphen and
an exclamation mark, like:

\bar staccis-1 {
    \inst1 c'4-! d'-! e'2
}

A staccatissimo note sounds for a percentage of its
duration, 25% by default. To change this percentage, use
\notedur.staccatissimo with an integer from 1 to 100:

\notedur.staccatissimo 15

This is applied to all instruments. See also \staccato
and \tenuto.
